<title>INDIA: India approves 350-mln-rupee GE subsidiary.</title>
<headline>India approves 350-mln-rupee GE subsidiary.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Indian Industry Ministry said on Wednesday that it approved a 350-million-rupee investment by a unit of U.S.-based General Electric Co (GE) in a lighting components subsidiary.  </p>
<p>The investment was among 58 proposals worth a total of 6.6 billion rupees which were approved by the Foreign Investment Promotion Board, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>It said GE Lighting (India) Ltd would set up the wholly-owned subsidiary in Bombay.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
